 "structural_change": "S81-TOPK9 LATTICE HARD-CHILD QUARTER (successor of hk1/hk1l after ROOT/Codex manual FAIL: 13/32 SRAM origins off the 43.2 lattice, std cells outside the band, and clock_spine whole-port ownership of the 16 K16 BUF roots that suppressed regional CTS -> WNS hold -656/-464 ps). Geometry = Codex literal32 model 1aa8f6744 (648x648, hist banks at its origins, 64.8 um full-width std band y302.4..367.2) with the SRAM stacks re-pitched so EVERY macro-macro gap is >= 20 um (the model's 5.9 / 3.2 um non-pin gaps fail ref_tile's channel rule): line words w0/w1 below the band at y43.2/172.8, w2 above at y388.8 (cols x388.8 / 518.4); OFQ0..3 y216 + OFQ4 (388.8,518.4); FQ0..3 y388.8 + FQ4 (475.2,518.4); all 32 origins on the literal 43.2 lattice, R0; corner reach to a band anchor <= 372.6 um (lines / OFQ / FQ); clock = TritonCTS under K16 k-means regional roots (no spine wrapper; hard-child insertion from the CLOSED view Liberty). Same RTL edges as hk1 (HQ3 + OT_HARD_CHILDREN). INPUT_RAW: raw type bits land at the first edge, decode after it (hk1l RTL, -21 FF, +0 edges).",
